# Lint suppression Beg Ritual

Until the user replies **yes / approved**, NEVER apply a suppression.

## Request template (all sections mandatory)

```markdown
## Lint suppression request (I failed to fix this properly)

I am asking permission to weaken enforcement. That is a last resort and a mark
against this change.

### What I broke / cannot satisfy

- **Tool + rule:** …
- **Location:** `path:line`
- **Exact diagnostic:** (paste)

### What I already tried

1. …
2. … (Real attempts only—not “it would be hard”.)

### Why a correct fix is not viable in this change

(Concrete constraint—not convenience.)

### What I want you to approve

- Exact artifact (single site)
- How we will remove it later

### Closing

I should have made the code satisfy the lint. I will not apply anything until
you say so.
```

## If rejected or silent

ALWAYS acknowledge, then try a **new** real fix (no re-beg without new attempts):

```markdown
## Suppression refused — I will fix it properly

You rejected (or did not approve) weakening the lint. That was the right call. I
was wrong to ask for an exception before exhausting a real fix. Next I will try:
(specific new approach). I will not add ignores.
```

## If accepted

- Rust: `#[expect(clippy::…, reason = "User-approved: <what>; chat approval <how>; remove when <condition>")]`
- Biome/ESLint: document approval in the ignore comment (`User-approved: …`) and
  a short allowlist note if the project has one.
- Python: `# type: ignore[code]  # User-approved: …` or
  `# noqa: CODE  # User-approved: …`
- NEVER silent `allow` / bare ignore.
